  ## Security review: frontend auth (creditsAI)
  
  Scope: I read the listed frontend files, their specs, `credits-realm.json`, and the keycloak-angular source (`frontend/node_modules/keycloak-angular/fesm2022/keycloak-angular.mjs`). I edited nothing and ran nothing. I did not run `npm audit` or the tests.
  
  ### What the library actually does (confirmed in source)
  - `findMatchingCondition` (line 1451) runs `urlPattern.test(req.url)` against `req.url` exactly as the caller passed it. Angular does not resolve the URL or make it absolute first. With the methods filter empty, every HTTP method matches.
  - `includeBearerTokenInterceptor` (line 1527) only touches requests that match a condition. Before attaching the token it calls `keycloak.updateToken()` with the default minValidity of 5s (line 1329). If the refresh fails, the error is swallowed and the current, possibly expired, token is sent anyway, so the backend answers 401.
  - `provideKeycloak` (line 1604) does register `options.providers`, so your `INCLUDE_BEARER_TOKEN_INTERCEPTOR_CONFIG` takes effect.
  - `keycloak.init()` failures are swallowed with `console.error` (line 1560). The app then starts unauthenticated.
  
  ### Findings
  
  | Severity | File:line | Issue | Fix |
  |---|---|---|---|
  | Medium | /Users/vbb/IdeaProjects/creditsAI/frontend/src/index.html:9-18 | Google Fonts (Roboto and Material Symbols) load from fonts.googleapis.com and fonts.gstatic.com. Every page load sends the user's IP and Referer to Google (a GDPR concern for a credit app). It also forces the CSP to allow third-party style and font origins. SRI can't help, because Google serves a different CSS file per user agent. | Self-host the fonts, for example with the npm packages `@fontsource/roboto` and `material-symbols` imported in `styles.scss`, or put the font files in `public/`. That lets the CSP stay `'self'`. Adding packages is a decision for the user. |
  | Medium (future nginx) | frontend/nginx.conf (not yet created) | The SPA has no CSP and no security headers yet. That matters most for an app that holds bearer tokens in JS memory, where XSS means token theft. | See the nginx checklist below. |
  | Low | /Users/vbb/IdeaProjects/creditsAI/keycloak/import/credits-realm.json:29 | `post.logout.redirect.uris: "http://localhost/*"` is wider than needed. The app only ever logs out to `http://localhost/` (auth.service.ts:34). The wildcard also accepts `/api/...` and `/auth/...` paths. This is same-origin only, so it is not an open redirect, but nothing needs it. | Set it to `"http://localhost/"` exactly. Re-importing needs the realm deleted or the volume reset, so ask the user first. |
